{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id112871595"}, "name":{"label":"_IantoJones"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-05-31T00:40:57-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"14126354019"}, "title":{"label":"Crashes and dumps the workout"}, "content":{"label":"The app frequently crashes mid (wheelchair) workout.  It dumps the entire workout instead of just stopping where it was.\n\nI’m a paid client (annual) and this is beyond infuriating; I’m looking for a different app, but admittedly this is one of the few that can measure wheelchair distance.\n\nBut that’s useless when it CRASHES and DUMPS.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id150645272"}, "name":{"label":"PatronOfSoftwareArts"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-05-30T05:15:19-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"14123133057"}, "title":{"label":"Extremely inaccurate data"}, "content":{"label":"I’ve had Pedometer++ on my iPhone for over 30 months now(on 3 different iPhones and 2 Apple Watches), and it’s typically off by thousands of steps each day vs. Apple’s Activity app. I wear my Apple Watch for the entirety of each day, so the Activity app represents the most accurate assessment of my activity for the day. \n\nPedometer++ typically shows 2x the steps that I’ve actually taken. Since this app fails at its primary purpose, I cannot personally recommend Pedometer++.\n\nI’m currently using said app on an iPhone XS Max and Series 4 Apple Watch.\n\nIf a future update begins counting my steps accurately, I’ll promptly update me review.\n\nUpdate: I decided to give this app another look to see if the accuracy has improved. In 2026, it’s still wildly inaccurate by thousands of steps each day. For example, per my Apple Watch - which is the gold standard for accuracy - I’ve been averaging just over 14,000 steps a day in May. Pedometer++ has me at 17,000-19,000 on days I actually walk 14,000.\n\nHow can you develop an app for so many years and never improve the accuracy? You’re much better off using data from your Apple Watch.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1374220611"}, "name":{"label":"just a fr0g fri3nd"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-05-28T07:06:02-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"14115765223"}, "title":{"label":"glitch"}, "content":{"label":"over counts steps, iphone health says 7k and watch says 10k but this says 25k and 199 stairs. i would know if i climbed almost 200 stairs lol 😭. also at one point everytime i refreshed it added 5k steps, started at 5,000 and left phone and watch to charge. came back to 20k, refreshed and it was 25k. everytime i rebooted or refreshed it just kept adding til i got to 55k.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id32016881"}, "name":{"label":"btakac"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-05-24T20:29:23-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"14102938548"}, "title":{"label":"Paid for it Once"}, "content":{"label":"I purchased this app once - a perpetual license. For life.\n\nThe developer forced users to upgrade to a monthly “service” because all of the benefits SAAS offers I guess (a predictable revenue stream for the developer)\n\nWhat happened to my perpetual  license?  \n\nI guess nothing if I enjoy limited functionality and the user interface littered with ad banners.\n\nI feel like I got screwed.\n\nToo bad about the product - I liked it a lot in its original form - not as a SAAS product. I'm surprised that you are not forced to pay based on the steps taken per month.\n\nDisgraceful.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
